map.gates:
All of these were run on 2026-10-02. Every gate passes in both trees, and check-publish passes as well.

- **tools/check.mjs** (in both trees; reads ../js relative to itself and ignores LEDGER_JS for the main load). It enforces:
  - 3 to 5 marks plus a fault per family, every family resolves, no mark names a drink, and forked marks carry a condition word;
  - LORE and COCKTAILS close over each other in both directions;
  - unique slugify routes per collection;
  - SHELF_PRESETS ids resolve;
  - every *_STUDY key is unique and every *_REF dom names a real section (SERVICE, ONTAP, COFFEE);
  - every coffee film's sec and row resolve, and data-coffee-films.js has no literal non-ASCII byte;
  - sw.js ASSETS and index.html agree in both directions;
  - TABS, views, NAV_CLUSTERS and ROUTE_SOURCES agree;
  - git: any cached asset committed since the last sw.js change, with CACHE unchanged, fails.
- **check-abv.mjs:** every measured strong line carries an ABV, non-alcoholic lines stay out of the spirit column, authored zeros survive, and an either/or takes the max.
- **check-ingredients.mjs:** every spec line in COCKTAILS, SHOTS and NA_DRINKS resolves to INGREDIENTS or NOTE_LINES; the vocabulary is well formed; every requirement is reachable; no drink needs nothing; the frozen migrateShelf list holds; the alcohol-free shelf claims only the Nojito.
- **check-levels.mjs** (identical in both trees). It checks:
  - every item is placed once, with a reason, under its own sub, and craft questions sit in CRAFT_SUBS;
  - the fixed books hold (tiers 1 and 2 at Barback, tier 3 at Bartender, nothing from tier 4 up at Barback);
  - BOOK_ORDER climbs by mean level;
  - data-levels.js is exactly what the placements emit, in pure ASCII;
  - SUPPLY per level: cocktails card 8, shots card 4, ontap card 2, ontap question 2, spirits question 3, technique question 2, stick question 6, prep question 2, coffee card 2; plus at least one met-able unit in every sub at every level;
  - every drill's ready figure appears in its desc;
  - LEVEL_TEST_SHAPE stays within SUPPLY.
- **check-home.mjs:** the home, the level pages and the level tests on three records:
  - 17 questions, the "What got away" ending with no score, and no numerals;
  - every door resolves;
  - no em dash in the screens' own words (content panels are excluded);
  - books named by name in BOOK_ORDER.
- **check-options.mjs:** pick-longest is at most 27%, and the share of unique-longest keys is at most 12.8% of the bank (floor 25). Now: standalone 13.0% and 23 of 37 allowed; suite 14.0% and 26 of 37 allowed.
- **check-import.mjs:** the menu parser and desk on node:test (0 failures).
- **check-years.mjs** (suite only): a drink's note years and lore years must agree.
- **check-films.mjs:** goes to YouTube over the network and is not a gate (18 play).
- **Suite publish gate** (OutsideOfTime/.scripts/check-publish.mjs):
  - LEDGER_GATES runs ledger/tools check-abv, check-ingredients, check, check-levels and check-home;
  - an em-dash count over the whole published tree (DASH matches U+2014, its entities, and " -- "), with DASH_BASELINE = 11. It stands at 10, so one dash of headroom is left for the entire suite. En dashes are not counted.

There are no known failures before this work. Caveats:
- No gate enforces "names no person" anywhere. It is an editorial rule only.
- Prose counts are ungated and already stale:
  - README.md says 196 questions; the bank holds 292.
  - CLAUDE.md says GLOSSARY has 68 terms; it has 132.
  - CLAUDE.md says COFFEE_REF is "not in DECK_SOURCES", which is now false.
  - index.html meta says "365 cocktail specs".
  - tools/levels/README.md gives 1,150 items, 674 cards, 365, 292 and 11 drills.

